{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n**Inputs are presented with the returned value's `NodeContents::format`.**\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` uses a formatter that changes the text to `formatted input: source`. It asserts that this text appears in the first user message, and that the node is read exactly once.\n- `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks that the rendered inputs reach the agent in queued order. They include repeated nodes and successor selections.\n- `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` checks that the domain's contents appear in the message in the expected order.\n- `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` uses `distinct_pages`, which produces formatted text. Its `ParallelConversations::complete` asserts that each `read_node` conversation history contains its own formatted content and not the other's. This covers the `read_node` tool path.\n\n**Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n- In `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot`, the underlying content is changed after the snapshot is taken. The snapshot's `format()` still returns `before`, and its `fingerprint()` still equals the snapshot's fingerprint, whose value is `before`.\n- The `source` fingerprint value, the `formatted input: source` text and the recorded dependency agree in `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix`.\n- `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` shows formatting uses only the retained value. It supplies a node whose file does not exist, and `format()` still returns the supplied text.\n\n**Failures from loading or preparation.**\n- For inputs queued on an ask builder, `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` covers both failure kinds. A read failure returns `ValidationError::Graph(\"read\")`. A preparation failure returns `ValidationError::Graph(\"render\")`, records no dependency, and makes no agent request.\n- During a `read_node` tool call, `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes preparation fail. It asserts the following:\n  - The tool result has `is_error` set.\n  - The tool name is `read_node`.\n  - The content is the error message.\n  - The agent then continues and submits a result.\n  - No dependency is recorded.\n- That test exercises preparation failure only, not load failure, on the `read_node` path. Load and preparation errors both come out of `Domain::node_content`'s `Err`. The distinction therefore adds no separate required behavior, and I did not count it as a gap.\n\nEverything else needed is covered by the cited requirements. The `NodeContents::format` contract is cited context and I did not reassess it.",
  "references": "8048d176a8293e95cc92aa446b4513cd36a149d6f42a172bff9e5eae9b604752",
